### GDScript script guide:

The following snippet shows the template for how the produces snippets should be:

```
# class name at the top of the file
class_name Lobby
extends Control

# Then any signal
signal on_host_pressed

# Then any const variable
const MY_VARIABLE := 0

# Then any @onready variable
@onready var host_button: Button = %HostButton

# Then any @export variable
@export var my_config := ""

# Then any built-in function
func _ready() -> void:

# Then any public function
func public_fn():

# Then any 'private' function
func _private_fn():

# Then any RPC when on multiplayer
@rpc("authority", "call_local", "reliable")
func remote_call() -> void:

# Then any signal or callback
func _on_signal_for_something() -> void:
```

### Variable naming convention

Following snippet shows the naming convention for variables:

```
extends CharacterBody2D

# const variables always uppercase
const SPEED := 220.0

# private/internal variables prepend with '_'
var _is_attacking := false

# public variables just the default snake case
var is_underwater := true
```

- All variables should be snake_case
- Everything should be typed
